    "independent": false,
    "summary": "Repaired the three failing app-server tests, then built the missing document-assistant frontend. Server: application service providers now tolerate a runtime composed without the optional authorization/AI-employee plugins, the documents seed encodes the Permission Set title as the JSON the store decodes, and the documents API scopes authentication to its own Repository action paths instead of a catch-all that swallowed unregistered /api requests. Frontend: registered the `materials` and `assistant` app routes with page authz ids matching the seed grants, added the document library page (read view for everyone, create/edit/delete gated on the `documents.materials` `manage` composite grant) and the read-only assistant page (advances from the AI configuration signal, no attachments or web search, and a clear unavailable state with a link to the library when no model is enabled), and added the en-US/zh-CN strings. Verified with the client-routes, route-navigation, plugin-page-authz, client-shell, locale-coverage and documents-api tests, client typecheck, scoped lint/format, and a full pnpm build.",
    "blockers": [],
    "improvements": [
      {
        "id": "notes/run/36938142232/attempt/1/I1",
        "category": "verification",
        "title": "Seed page-grant ids had no matching route",
        "detail": "The documents seed granted page access to ids \"materials\" and \"assistant\", but no route declared those page ids, so the Users Permissions list showed an empty page section and the pages were unreachable until client/routes.ts declared matching authz ids.",
